      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the base 7 numbers \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) to base 10.\n2. Compute their product in base 10.\n3. Convert the product back to base 7.\n4. Find the sum of the digits of the base 7 product.\n\n**Step 1: Convert \\(24_7\\) to base 10.**\n\nThe number \\(24_7\\) can be expanded as:\n\\[2 \\cdot 7^1 + 4 \\cdot 7^0 = 2 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot 1 = 14 + 4 = 18_{10}.\\]\n\n**Step 2: Convert \\(30_7\\) to base 10.**\n\nThe number \\(30_7\\) can be expanded as:\n\\[3 \\cdot 7^1 + 0 \\cdot 7^0 = 3 \\cdot 7 + 0 \\cdot 1 = 21 + 0 = 21_{10}.\\]\n\n**Step 3: Compute the product in base 10.**\n\nNow, we multiply the two base 10 numbers:\n\\[18 \\times 21 = 378.\\]\n\n**Step 4: Convert \\(378_{10}\\) back to base 7.**\n\nTo convert \\(378_{10}\\) to base 7, we divide by 7 and keep track of the remainders:\n\\[378 \\div 7 = 54 \\text{ remainder } 0,\\]\n\\[54 \\div 7 = 7 \\text{ remainder } 5,\\]\n\\[7 \\div 7 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 0,\\]\n\\[1 \\div 7 = 0 \\text{ remainder } 1.\\]\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get \\(378_{10} = 1050_7\\).\n\n**Step 5: Find the sum of the digits of the base 7 product.**\n\nThe digits of \\(1050_7\\) are 1, 0, 5, and 0. The sum of these digits is:\n\\[1 + 0 + 5 + 0 = 6.\\]\n\nTherefore, the base seven sum of the digits of the product is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
