      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we will first convert the base 7 numbers \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) to base 10, perform the multiplication in base 10, convert the result back to base 7, and finally find the sum of the digits of the resulting base 7 number.\n\n**Step 1: Convert \\(24_7\\) to base 10.**\n\nThe base 7 number \\(24_7\\) can be expanded as:\n\\[2 \\cdot 7^1 + 4 \\cdot 7^0 = 2 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot 1 = 14 + 4 = 18_{10}.\\]\n\n**Step 2: Convert \\(30_7\\) to base 10.**\n\nThe base 7 number \\(30_7\\) can be expanded as:\n\\[3 \\cdot 7^1 + 0 \\cdot 7^0 = 3 \\cdot 7 + 0 \\cdot 1 = 21 + 0 = 21_{10}.\\]\n\n**Step 3: Multiply the base 10 equivalents.**\n\nNow, we multiply the two base 10 numbers:\n\\[18 \\cdot 21 = 378.\\]\n\n**Step 4: Convert \\(378_{10}\\) back to base 7.**\n\nTo convert \\(378_{10}\\) to base 7, we repeatedly divide by 7 and keep track of the remainders:\n\\[378 \\div 7 = 54 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0,\\]\n\\[54 \\div 7 = 7 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 5,\\]\n\\[7 \\div 7 = 1 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0,\\]\n\\[1 \\div 7 = 0 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 1.\\]\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get the base 7 number \\(1050_7\\).\n\n**Step 5: Find the sum of the digits of \\(1050_7\\).**\n\nThe digits of \\(1050_7\\) are 1, 0, 5, and 0. The sum of these digits is:\n\\[1 + 0 + 5 + 0 = 6.\\]\n\nTherefore, the base seven sum of the digits of the product is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
